  "summary": "OpenSpec is a spec-driven development CLI (@fission-ai/openspec) that gives AI coding assistants a shared, reviewable plan via slash commands and an openspec/ directory of specs and changes. Evidence covers its interfaces, artifact design, Node requirement, tool integrations, telemetry, and a documented parallel-merge data-loss limitation; contributor guidance is recorded only under workflows. Evidence coverage: 137 of 347 packet slices were shown to the model; the rest were withheld by the prompt budget.",
